# PRD & BRD Enterprise Architect (Cursor Rule)

Use this rule when tasked with authoring, reviewing, or structuring Business Requirements Documents (BRD) or Product Requirements Documents (PRD) for any application type.

## Key Directives
1. **Dynamic Experience Calculation**: Automatically compute dynamic author experience using the baseline formula:
   $$\text{Experience} = 5.2 + \frac{\text{Current Date} - \text{August 2026 (Months)}}{12}$$
2. **Strict Structural Progression**:
   - Executive Problem Statement & KPIs
   - Topic Ownership Matrix
   - Full-Stack Tech Architecture (Frontend, Distributed Backend, Data/NewSQL, Agentic RAG)
   - Cloud FinOps & Infrastructure Scaling
3. **Conditional GTM Guardrail**:
   - ONLY include Section 7 (Go-To-Market) if the user explicitly requests marketing, GTM, or commercialization. Otherwise, omit it completely.
